public/weather/*/
# Small real ECMWF acceptance snapshot; later generated runs stay ignored.
!public/weather/ecmwf-2026091300-360h-v1/
!public/weather/ecmwf-2026091300-360h-v2/
# Small real GFS acceptance snapshot (2026-09-16 12 UTC, 120 h at 3-hour steps).
!public/weather/gfs-2026091612-120h-v1/
# Small real ICON-EU surface weather acceptance snapshot (2026-09-16 18 UTC, two
# frames at 3-hour steps). A weather frame is five arrays over 56,817 cells, about
# 1.25 MB, so the default 72-hour run is 30 MB and is generated locally.
!public/weather/icon-eu-weather-2026091618-3h-v1/
# Small real GFS-Wave acceptance snapshot (2026-09-16 18 UTC, 9 h at 3-hour steps).
# Wave frames carry nine variables over 121 × 101 cells, so a longer bundled run
# would be tens of megabytes; generate one locally for real use.
!public/weather/gfs-wave-2026091618-9h-v1/
# Small real ARPEGE acceptance snapshot (2026-09-16 18 UTC, 12 h at 3-hour steps).
# An ARPEGE frame is three arrays over 22,311 cells, about 360 KB, so the default
# 102-hour run is 12 MB and is generated locally.
!public/weather/arpege-2026091618-12h-v1/
# Generated AROME output. A 0.025° frame is 600 KB over 35,787 cells and three of
# the 25 riding locations fall outside the model, so no snapshot is bundled.
public/weather/arome.json
# Generated tide predictions; nothing marine is bundled yet.
public/marine/
# Generated wave forecast; no wave snapshot is bundled with the site.
public/weather/mi-swan.json
# Generated ensemble manifests: they carry every member and are far too large
# to bundle, so no snapshot of either is committed.
public/weather/gefs.json
public/weather/ecmwf-ens.json
*.tsbuildinfo
